00:59:36.360 --> 00:59:39.040
So don't feel like you
have to ask a question

00:59:39.040 --> 00:59:41.360
or a comment that is highly impressive.

00:59:41.360 --> 00:59:44.990
So I think Rob Comans has a question

00:59:44.990 --> 00:59:47.630
who said that I still need to dive

00:59:47.630 --> 00:59:49.050
into professor Ay's work here

00:59:49.050 --> 00:59:52.860
but do you have any comments
on causal information theory?

00:59:52.860 --> 00:59:54.530
Is this field well developed

00:59:54.530 --> 00:59:57.240
or are there good reasons
that information theory

00:59:57.240 --> 00:59:58.840
is less useful

00:59:58.840 --> 01:00:01.823
or relevant with
interventional distributions?

01:00:03.640 --> 01:00:05.050
- So that's a very good question.

01:00:05.050 --> 01:00:10.050
So I think they are tightly
coupled the two theories.

01:00:10.970 --> 01:00:15.970
So originally when information
theory was invented

01:00:17.280 --> 01:00:21.590
by Claude Shannon, he
considered actually channel.

01:00:21.590 --> 01:00:26.413
Channel, that's the term
for a mark of counter

01:00:29.890 --> 01:00:32.540
or the stochastic map.

01:00:32.540 --> 01:00:33.640
So that's the mechanism.

01:00:33.640 --> 01:00:35.970
So he did consider mechanisms.

01:00:35.970 --> 01:00:40.970
But it was a very simple
setting, sender and receiver.

01:00:42.010 --> 01:00:45.110
Okay, so you have X and Y
and then you have the arrow

01:00:45.110 --> 01:00:48.050
between them and you can
compute the mutual information.

01:00:48.050 --> 01:00:52.000
The fundamental quantity there
is the mutual information.

01:00:52.000 --> 01:00:55.380
And the mutual information is a kind of

01:00:55.380 --> 01:00:59.100
or mutual information rate
is a kind of a measure

01:00:59.100 --> 01:01:01.773
for the information flow from X to Y.

01:01:02.910 --> 01:01:07.910
Now, if you have the situation
that Kyle was referring to

01:01:11.687 --> 01:01:13.450
where you have a common cause.

01:01:13.450 --> 01:01:15.420
Let's say you have X, Y

01:01:15.420 --> 01:01:18.550
but they are influenced by Z, okay?

01:01:18.550 --> 01:01:21.110
And there is no cause information flow

01:01:21.110 --> 01:01:24.950
from X to Y but they are correlated.

01:01:24.950 --> 01:01:28.130
So if you compute the mutual
information between X and Y,

01:01:28.130 --> 01:01:29.900
you will get a positive quantity

01:01:31.030 --> 01:01:33.030
but you would then assume, okay,

01:01:33.030 --> 01:01:35.933
there is information flow
from X to Y which is wrong.

01:01:37.280 --> 01:01:42.280
Okay, but then the way we
correct this is the following.

01:01:42.280 --> 01:01:45.990
We say, okay, instead of
measuring the joint distribution

01:01:45.990 --> 01:01:48.040
of X and Y by just observing it,

01:01:48.040 --> 01:01:51.603
we have to intervene in X and observe Y.

01:01:52.530 --> 01:01:54.580
And then you do this in the context

01:01:54.580 --> 01:01:56.630
of this common cause example,

01:01:56.630 --> 01:01:58.880
so Z is acting on X and Y.

01:01:58.880 --> 01:02:03.610
You intervene in X and the
condition distribution of Y

01:02:03.610 --> 01:02:06.370
given X is simply the distribution of Y

01:02:06.370 --> 01:02:09.030
because it does not depend on X anymore

01:02:09.030 --> 01:02:12.090
and the reason is that there
is no arrow from X to Y.

01:02:12.090 --> 01:02:16.800
So if you do the
interventional conditioning,

01:02:16.800 --> 01:02:18.263
you get the mark of counter,

01:02:19.270 --> 01:02:22.940
a channel that has no
information flow from X to Y.

01:02:22.940 --> 01:02:26.350
And if you then, after
intervening in this,

01:02:26.350 --> 01:02:29.720
after changing the notion of conditioning

01:02:29.720 --> 01:02:31.740
then use information theory

01:02:31.740 --> 01:02:36.570
then you get the real notion
of causal information flow.

01:02:36.570 --> 01:02:39.510
So combining the notion of intervention

01:02:39.510 --> 01:02:44.270
with classical information
theory gives you a nice formalism

01:02:44.270 --> 01:02:47.000
to quantify cause and information flows.

01:02:47.000 --> 01:02:48.440
And this is what I did together

01:02:48.440 --> 01:02:50.563
with Daniel Polanyi actually.

